      {
        "id": 103933,
        "name": "jagarciao",
        "username": "jagarciao",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jagarciao/{size}/2010_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-05-20T12:46:35.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"LevelUpLeo\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/levelupleo/48/2394_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> LevelUpLeo:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The wording is different though. Stealth reads\"Reduce the next damage that would be dealt to the Wraith by 2\"This is clear that the next 1 instance of damage would be reduced by 2.The ability being discussed reads\"Prevent the next 2 damage dealt to that hero\"As the OP pointed out, its really ambugious compared to other similar abilities. Doesn't say that it only activates the next time a hero would be damage, just \"the next 2 damage\". Sounds to me like it could prevent 1 damage from 1 attack, and then another 1 damage from another attack as those would be the next 2 damage dealt to that hero.&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I would have to agree that the way it is written it prevents the next two damage whether they come in a single instance or in different instances. It also doesn't seem like it would be stackable. Only the next 2 damage would be prevented regardless of how many times the incapacitated power was activated</p>",
