      {
        "id": 103938,
        "name": "LevelUpLeo",
        "username": "LevelUpLeo",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/levelupleo/{size}/2394_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-05-21T01:32:48.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"jagarciao\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jagarciao/48/2010_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> jagarciao:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Hmmmm. I think that may be the difference between \"reduce by\" (which I think of as subtract from) and \"prevent\" (which I see as imagine it just doesn't exist)… Although since nothing really happens simultaneously in this game the I imagine 3 instances of \"Prevent 2\" applied in succession could logically be equivalent to \"Prevent 6\"… so I guess the argument could go either way…</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I am as confused as ever to how this power would work, I'm actually on the fence on both how many times it will prevent damage (either just the next instance or until it presents everything promised) and how much it will prevent (always 2 or 2 for each time it was used since).</p>",
        "post_number": 27,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:33:11.805Z",
