      {
        "id": 103939,
        "name": "The Orange Mailman",
        "username": "The_Orange_Mailman",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/c68b51/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-10-26T21:04:57.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Got this game about a month ago.&nbsp; I'm really enjoying it, but struggling with a couple of issues.&nbsp; Reading through the forums helps some, but it's obvious this game is pretty new by some standards.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Was there ever an official ruling on this?&nbsp; Is it the next two damage, as in the next two damages, or the next two damage on the next instance of damage?</p><p>The other night I had 3 heroes and Bunker and Haka both bit the dust.&nbsp; So I had Bunker's incapacitated power of \"Prevent the next two damage dealt to that hero\" along with Haka's \"decrease the next damage ... by two.\"</p><p>What would be a good pragmatic way to track both of these powers as they stack?&nbsp; And how is each one dealt with differently?&nbsp; I took a \"Immune to Damage\" token and stacked counters on top of it for Bunker's, and then I took a \"Takes -1 Damage\" and stacked counters on top of that for Haka's.&nbsp; In what instances&nbsp;are each one \"wiped\" and in what instances do counters come off individually?&nbsp; Thanks in advance.</p>",
        "post_number": 28,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:33:11.903Z",
